    rule2Text: "Each magnetron waveguide must be isolated by a 3-port junction ferrite circulator with minimum 20 dB isolation connected to a dedicated deionized water dummy load. In vacuum microwave drying, as food moisture evaporates and dielectric loss factor (ε″) collapses from >20 down to <0.5, cavity impedance shifts rapidly, reflecting up to 45% of incident microwave power. Without circulator redirection into chilled water loads, reflected microwaves return directly into the magnetron antenna dome, causing thermal cathode expansion, catastrophic mode hopping, and premature tube failure.",
