    rule3Text: "Operating chamber vacuum pressure must be maintained within the 30 to 60 mbar process window. Pressures below 20 mbar plunge the atmosphere directly into the Townsend breakdown trough where plasma ignition risk is maximal. Conversely, operating above 80 mbar raises moisture boiling saturation temperature above 45°C to 50°C, inducing severe thermal degradation of heat-sensitive bioactive phytochemicals (anthocyanins, polyphenols, enzymes, and probiotic cultures).",
    rule4Title: "OSHA 1910.97 Non-Ionizing Microwave Radiation Leakage Limits",
    rule4Text: "Under OSHA 1910.97 and FDA 21 CFR § 1030.10, stray microwave radiation leakage around vacuum lock rotary valves, inspection quartz sight glasses, and waveguide flanges must never exceed 5.0 mW/cm² measured at 5 cm from outer surfaces (and 10 mW/cm² workplace ceiling). All access hatches must be interlocked with dual Category 4 safety switches, and continuous perimeter RF sniffer sensors must be integrated into the PLC emergency stop loop.",
